Create one production-ready transparent frame asset for the Urkaaaz match HUD,
refining the lightweight frame treatment in the latest approved HUD mockup.
The same asset must Nine-patch scale for the complete bottom dock, both
fortress HP cards, and the central timer/wind/pause panel.

This deliverable is one standalone frame image only. Do not create a screen
mockup, separate frame variants, Android UI, or gameplay graphics.

## Reference input

Attach the latest approved full-screen Urkaaaz match HUD mockup. Use it as the
style reference for the thin bronze-gold edge, rounded geometry, and restrained
warm highlights. Do not copy its text, icons, panel fill, or battlefield into
the asset.

Do not attach the older thick gold frames or earlier heavy HUD mockups; they
conflict with this direction.

## Output

- Filename: `match_hud_universal_frame.png`
- Source path: `assets_src/match/hud/match_hud_universal_frame.png`
- Canvas: exactly 512 x 190 pixels, landscape, approximately 2.7:1.
- Format: RGBA PNG.
- Return exactly one standalone asset.
- Do not include Nine-patch guide pixels or markers; Android markers are added
  separately after the art is reviewed.

## Visual design

- Create a clean horizontal rounded-rectangle frame with a single, fine
  bronze-gold edge. Match the latest mockup's lighter treatment; keep the
  border visibly slimmer than the older universal frame.
- Use one restrained warm highlight along the edge for a crafted Urkaaaz
  fantasy character. Avoid a double rail, deep bevel, bright continuous gold
  outline, glow, ornament, rivets, diamonds, spikes, or a bulky plaque look.
- Keep both outer and inner contours smoothly rounded. Use compact corners
  that stay balanced on short HP and timer panels.
- Keep the long straight edge sections and center low-detail so they stretch
  cleanly. Preserve border thickness and corner shape through Nine-patch
  resizing.
- The frame must work on panels with very different proportions: compact
  fortress HP cards and center timer, as well as the wide bottom dock.
- Use one neutral, symmetric design. Do not imply BLUE, RED, Supply, Mana,
  ammunition, spells, or any other HUD section.

## Transparency and runtime content

- The entire panel interior must be fully transparent (alpha 0).
- Pixels outside the rounded frame silhouette must be fully transparent.
- Draw only the frame itself. Do not include panel fill, texture, shadow, text,
  numbers, icons, dividers, labels, controls, or values.
- Android renders a separate shared panel surface of `#1A1A1A` at 80% opacity
  (`#CC` alpha) beneath the frame.
- Android draws the dock's internal separators and all dynamic content above
  the surface. Do not bake these into the asset.
- Do not add a shadow; the Android UI supplies it separately.

## Reuse targets

The same PNG is used for:

1. The complete bottom command dock as one outer frame around Supply/units/
   Send Wave, ammunition, and spells/Mana. Internal group separators are
   separate UI elements; do not split the dock into three framed boxes.
2. The BLUE fortress HP card.
3. The RED fortress HP card.
4. The central timer/wind/pause panel. Keep the pause control inside this
   panel, separated from the timer/wind area by exactly one subtle vertical
   divider drawn by Android. The divider is a separate UI element, not part of
   the frame PNG.

No target-specific or team-specific variants are needed.

## Negative requirements

- No opaque or translucent fill in the image; panel fill remains a separate
  Android layer.
- No black canvas background, padded square canvas, or small frame centered
  inside the canvas.
- No text, labels, numbers, logos, icons, team colors, health bars, slot
  borders, buttons, separators, or other UI contents.
- No thick double outlines, excessive gold, bright neon, heavy texture, deep
  bevel, angular/chamfered corners, spikes, bulky ornaments, or contact sheet.

## Review checklist

- Confirm the file is one valid 512 x 190 RGBA PNG with the exact filename.
- Confirm both the panel interior and exterior are fully transparent.
- Confirm the edge is single, slim, softly rounded, and visually consistent
  with the latest approved mockup.
- Preview the same Nine-patch around the complete bottom dock, both short HP
  cards, and the center timer panel; do not alter the source asset between
  previews.
- Confirm corner shape and border thickness stay balanced at the shortest
  target height and that only straight edge sections and the plain center
  stretch.
- Do not integrate the asset into Android until it is reviewed and approved.
